WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.800
From characters surviving fatal&nbsp;
wounds to zombies with super speed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.220
there are still some aspects of&nbsp;
"The Walking Dead" that simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:13.260
can't be explained. Here are just some of the&nbsp;
strange inconsistencies and giant plot holes.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.360
In the very first episode, Rick Grimes&nbsp;
awakes from a coma to find himself in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:22.740
the middle of a zombie apocalypse. While this&nbsp;
certainly makes for a dramatic series kickoff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:28.680
it's never made clear how Rick managed to survive&nbsp;
up to that point. Prior to the apocalypse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:33.540
Rick was a sheriff's deputy. He sustained a&nbsp;
gunshot wound in the line of duty, which put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:38.220
him in a coma for four to five weeks, according&nbsp;
to "Walking Dead" showrunner Dave Erickson.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:43.560
That's a lot of time to be in a coma without&nbsp;
medical attention. In the web series, "The Oath",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.220
we learn that a doctor stayed at the&nbsp;
hospital after the outbreak and took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.840
care of the patients for a while.
 
"My oath is to people who need help,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.180
and that holds up now, more than ever."

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:03.000
This helps explain how Rick survived, but&nbsp;
he still wakes up alone and malnourished,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.720
which implies that he's been without&nbsp;
medical care for a while. It must be magic.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:11.700
The outbreak happens on August 26, 2010,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:17.880
yet Rick and the gang somehow find a 2011&nbsp;
Hyundai Tucson in Season 2. This means that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.840
the group found a vehicle that wasn't&nbsp;
invented yet, let alone mass-produced.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:27.720
They drive the kiwi green SUV around for two&nbsp;
seasons, using it to escape from hordes of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:32.280
zombies, but it never gets a dent or a&nbsp;
speck of blood on it. The vehicle stays&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:36.420
sparkling clean in a post-apocalyptic world&nbsp;
because of a product placement deal with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:41.400
Hyundai. The contract stated that the vehicle&nbsp;
couldn't break down, get excessively dirty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:47.280
or be used to run over zombies. While this makes&nbsp;
sense for Hyundai, the pristine car looks out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.960
of place in the world of the show. But hey, if&nbsp;
we were living in a post-apocalyptic world and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.220
found a time-traveling car that was always clean&nbsp;
and never broke down, we'd drive it around, too.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:01.620
Rick and the rest of the survivors are in&nbsp;
Georgia for most of the series. Georgia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:06.540
summers are hot and humid, but it gets&nbsp;
cold and snows during winter. Despite this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:10.200
we hardly ever see the survivors&nbsp;
deal with snow in "The Walking Dead".

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.040
In fact, there isn't a single&nbsp;
snowflake until the Season 9 finale.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.980
"The best bet is to go old&nbsp;
school to keep toasty. I'd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.140
advise initiating Winter I - Ice Storm Protocol."

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:23.580
In 2022, showrunner Angela Kang told CinemaBlend,

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:27.840
"One of the things we were trying to do&nbsp;
this season is play with the rhythm of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.320
the storytelling a little bit, and hopefully&nbsp;
do some things that we hadn't done before."

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:36.960
Between fending off walkers and hostile groups of&nbsp;
people, the characters already have a lot to deal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:42.240
with, but seeing them brave the elements upped&nbsp;
the ante even more. Since snowfall only adds to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.380
the drama, it's interesting that so little&nbsp;
of the show takes place during wintertime.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:53.040
In Season 8, Negan devises a plan for his&nbsp;
group to smear zombie guts on their weapons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:56.340
infecting anyone unlucky&nbsp;
enough to be attacked by them.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:02.940
"Hilltop is gonna learn to tow the line,&nbsp;
one way or another, dead or alive."

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.880
It sounds like a pretty good plan — except that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:09.780
reveals a huge plot hole about whether&nbsp;
or not zombie blood can infect people.

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:15.480
If survivors get infected every time zombie&nbsp;
DNA enters their bloodstream, there are several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:20.940
instances in which characters should've gotten&nbsp;
infected, but somehow don't. In Season 2, Episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:27.240
10, "18 Miles Out", Shane gets trapped in a school&nbsp;
bus while fighting walkers. He cuts his hand with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:33.600
a dirty knife and uses his blood to distract them.&nbsp;
In Season 7, Episode 10, "New Best Friends", Rick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:39.060
goes up against a walker with spikes coming out of&nbsp;
its body. His hand gets cut by one of the blades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:43.800
which we can assume is covered in infected&nbsp;
blood since it's impaling the zombie's body.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:47.100
So which is it? Can zombie&nbsp;
blood infect survivors or not?

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:50.220
"You all submit to a blood test.&nbsp;
That's the price of admission."

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:56.340
If not, Negan's plan makes no sense. And&nbsp;
another thing: why haven't survivors smeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:00.840
zombie goo on themselves more often to&nbsp;
avoid danger? They use this tactic to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:05.220
camouflage themselves in Seasons 1 and 5.&nbsp;
And of course, there are the Whisperers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:09.660
who regularly wear zombie faces to&nbsp;
blend in with herds of the undead.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:16.140
From the group's invincible Hyundai Tucson to&nbsp;
Daryl's iconic motorcycle, the survivors use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:20.460
a variety of vehicles throughout the show. But&nbsp;
the story takes place over a number of years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:25.140
and gasoline has an expiration date,&nbsp;
so where is this magic gas coming from?

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:28.500
RAC Limited, a British&nbsp;
automotive services company,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:31.560
confirmed this information in 2019, saying,

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:36.780
"Generally speaking, petrol has a shelf-life of&nbsp;
six months if stored in a sealed container at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:41.280
20 degrees [Celsius] — or just three&nbsp;
months if kept at 30 degrees. Once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:45.000
you've put fuel in a jerry can or other&nbsp;
containers, you only have a few months&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:49.320
before the quality starts to fall away —&nbsp;
even less if the fuel is contaminated."

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:54.720
They go on to explain that using old gasoline&nbsp;
can damage vehicles and impact their overall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:59.400
performance. However, this isn't the only reason&nbsp;
why characters shouldn't be able to drive in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:04.680
the show. Think about how much maintenance&nbsp;
vehicles require on a regular basis. Flat tires,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:08.640
dead batteries, and transmission problems&nbsp;
are pretty common problems even during a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:12.420
non-apocalypse. When you consider that&nbsp;
most of the vehicles in the show have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:16.860
been sitting unattended for months or years&nbsp;
on end, and not every group has a mechanic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:20.580
watching the survivors cruise&nbsp;
around at will just doesn't add up.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:26.820
Survivors in a post-apocalyptic world would&nbsp;
have way more to worry about than landscaping,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:30.720
so why are there freshly mowed lawns&nbsp;
in the show? The prison that Rick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:34.380
and the gang discover in Season 3&nbsp;
has a large, well-maintained yard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:38.700
despite no one taking care of it. There are&nbsp;
some prisoners there when the group arrives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:43.140
but they've been locked in the cafeteria for&nbsp;
months, so they didn't have access to the lawn.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:46.080
Was there a zombie landscaper&nbsp;
that still had the basic motor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.380
skills to push a lawnmower across&nbsp;
the field? Before the show aired,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:54.360
AMC released some rules that all zombies in&nbsp;
the show follow, which included this one:

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:57.780
"Zombies are not dexterous.&nbsp;
They cannot pick up or use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:00.420
any items more complex than a rock or a stick."

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.880
So no weed-whackers, then.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:07.200
During an interview with Chris&nbsp;
Hardwick in 2017, showrunner Scott&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:13.680
M. Gimple finally addressed this enigma: 
 "I am working on a story. All of these years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.620
why the grass is cut will be&nbsp;
answered. [...] It will be told."

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:21.060
It seems like it'd be hard to carve out "me&nbsp;
time" in the middle of a zombie apocalypse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:26.160
yet, between making supply runs and fighting for&nbsp;
their lives, the survivors manage to maintain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:31.680
stylish haircuts. Carol, for example, rocks a&nbsp;
pixie cut and Negan shaves the sides of his head.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:35.700
For the most part, the men do a great job&nbsp;
grooming their facial hair, whether they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:40.920
sporting a majestic, well-moisturized beard or&nbsp;
just the right amount of stubble. But the ladies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:45.480
of the show stay especially well-groomed. In&nbsp;
addition to keeping their eyebrows on point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:49.200
there aren't any hairy legs or&nbsp;
armpits in sight. Their smooth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:54.360
radiant skin hints at a 10-step nightly routine&nbsp;
and an effortless "no makeup" makeup look.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:58.740
No matter how dire the situation, all&nbsp;
of the survivors have stylish clothes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:02.400
that fit them perfectly. Yes, they're a&nbsp;
bit dirty and have some holes in them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.580
but that kind of wear and tear could&nbsp;
happen over the course of a week-long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:09.600
camping trip. And can we talk about how&nbsp;
great everyone's teeth look? Maybe there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:13.980
were salons and dentists in Alexandria, but&nbsp;
the rest of the time? It doesn't make sense.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:19.800
There are many different types of walkers in&nbsp;
the show, from those that couldn't move around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:25.560
to those that wandered back home, and everything&nbsp;
in between. But, despite all the zombie variants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:29.280
zombie children are weirdly missing&nbsp;
from the series for the most part.

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:34.560
Ironically, the first zombie that ever appears&nbsp;
on the show is a little girl. In the very first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:38.700
episode, Rick tries talking to her, but&nbsp;
then she starts getting aggressive and he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:42.480
has to shoot her. After that, there&nbsp;
are a handful of other zombie kids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:47.760
such as Carol's daughter Sophia, the Governor's&nbsp;
daughter Penny, and Noah's unnamed brother.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:51.420
However, that's nothing compared&nbsp;
to the hordes of adult zombies that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:55.920
threaten the survivors at every turn. The&nbsp;
scarcity of zombie children is unusual,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:58.800
especially considering that in&nbsp;
the "Walking Dead" universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:04.140
everyone has the virus and turns into a zombie&nbsp;
after they die, whether or not they're bitten.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:08.400
The survivors face all kinds of&nbsp;
danger throughout the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:13.260
including the possibility of starvation. At&nbsp;
the beginning of Season 3, the group has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:18.180
on the run for a while and Carl is so hungry&nbsp;
that he almost resorts to eating canned dog&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:22.680
food. There have even been episodes when the&nbsp;
group has to walk miles on end, like when they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:27.780
are trying to find Terminus in Season 4, but all&nbsp;
that extra cardio doesn't lead to any weight loss.

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:32.520
When it comes to body weight, viewers have had&nbsp;
questions about two characters in particular:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:38.820
Tara and Eugene. In a 2016 Instagram&nbsp;
post, Alanna Masterson, who played Tara,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:43.440
fired back at body shamers and explained&nbsp;
that she'd just had a baby before filming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:47.880
Season 7. Josh McDermitt, who played&nbsp;
Eugene, addressed his own character's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:51.900
appearance during an interview with&nbsp;
Entertainment Weekly in 2018, saying,

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:54.360
"It's hard to go from one&nbsp;
week to the next and you go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:58.200
'Well, it would be awesome if I was 30 pounds&nbsp;
lighter.' [...] That's physically impossible."

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:02.760
No one is saying that actors should be body&nbsp;
shamed or pressured to lose weight. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:08.640
when the story of the show involves extremely&nbsp;
meager rations and grueling journeys on foot, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:13.500
little makeup or CGI to temporarily slim down the&nbsp;
characters would make things much more realistic.

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:20.760
Is Rick immortal? He's survived the bleakest of&nbsp;
situations, like the bridge incident in Season 9,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:26.400
Episode 5, "What Comes After". He's bleeding&nbsp;
heavily after being thrown off his horse and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:32.220
impaled by a rebar in the previous episode.&nbsp;
Fading in and out of consciousness, he leads a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:37.200
huge herd of walkers to a bridge and sets off an&nbsp;
explosion to protect the rest of the survivors.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:42.240
But he's on the bridge with the herd when this&nbsp;
happens, so his friends and family assume he died&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:48.300
in the explosion. We later learn that Rick somehow&nbsp;
survived the blast, fell into the zombie-infested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:53.340
river below, and washed up on shore without&nbsp;
drowning, getting bitten, or losing a critical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:57.360
amount of blood. We get that the writers didn't&nbsp;
want to kill Rick off since he's the main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:02.460
character, but it's ridiculous how many injuries&nbsp;
this man can recover from. Any side character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:07.620
would've died as soon as they fell onto the rebar,&nbsp;
or at the very latest, during the explosion.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:13.920
Most of the walkers in the show are weak,&nbsp;
slow, unintelligent, and uncoordinated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:18.780
especially compared to the zombies in&nbsp;
franchises like "28 Days Later". Despite this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:23.400
there are many instances when the zombies&nbsp;
act differently than usual. Some of them are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:28.320
strong enough to single-handedly crack glass,&nbsp;
break through walls, or drag a grown man away.

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:33.000
When it comes to speed, AMC's rules for&nbsp;
the show state that zombies can't sprint;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:38.100
the fastest they can move is a, quote,&nbsp;
"shambling run." In addition, they explain that:

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:41.640
"The ability to run is based on&nbsp;
the amount of time a zombie has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:44.400
been undead, and how much decay has set in."

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:50.040
However, there have been times when walkers keep&nbsp;
pace with characters running at full speed. One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:54.960
glaring example of this is in the Season&nbsp;
2 premiere, "What Lies Ahead," when Sophia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:58.680
is running for her life and two walkers&nbsp;
are able to keep up with her just fine.

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:04.320
And what about the zombies' varying levels of&nbsp;
intelligence and dexterity? In the show's first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:09.000
episode, a zombie returns home and tries&nbsp;
to open the door. In the next episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:14.100
a zombie chasing after Rick and Glenn has&nbsp;
the wherewithal to climb over a chain link&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:19.140
fence without breaking its legs. These&nbsp;
instances are a far cry from walkers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:23.520
mindlessly stumbling around all day.&nbsp;
Do we chalk it up to undead evolution?

